{
  "date": "2026-10-25",
  "scope": "Actual GC I/O Result classification, unlink and parent sync/repair dispatch, and the production ordered ancestor-barrier loop. Conditional proofs do not establish native namespace/handle binding or aggregate repair durability.",
  "properties": {
    "gc_io::classify": "Successful I/O returns its original value. Only an error satisfying the explicit NotFound predicate becomes None; every other error propagates unchanged.",
    "gc_io::unlink": "Stat supplies advisory accounting only. Every successful deletion dispatch performs unlink on the resolved marked target, including stale/missing stat responses, and returns the bound parent. Failures may have effects but preserve batch identity, receipts and previously durable absence.",
    "gc_io::sync_parent": "After all targets are currently absent, synchronize the opened matching parent or successfully repair a missing parent before returning success. Errors cannot authorize success; successful hooks preserve modeled state.",
    "directory_io::sync_all": "For any finite supplied directory sequence, success attempts each barrier in order and establishes synchronization for all members. Failure attempts an exact nonempty prefix and preserves all successful earlier barriers. Existing directories receive barriers on every retry; neither existence nor a partial previous attempt permits skipping ancestors."
  },
  "runtime_changes": "Native BatchIo delegates actual deletion and parent dispatch to gc_io; its standard-I/O wrappers use the verified Result classifier. mkdir_with_sync delegates its existing ancestor vector and callback to directory_io::sync_all. The existing path resolution, create/canonicalize/enumeration, filesystem calls, callbacks and ordering are retained. This extraction adds no allocation or syscall, but does not establish a measured latency/throughput guarantee. No new production defect is claimed.",
  "boundaries": [
    "ENV-GC-PRIMITIVES explicitly supplies stable marked-target/path/parent binding, truthful unlink and directory-handle synchronization, monotonic durable absence and legal fault callbacks. Failed primitives may have effects or lose transient absence.",
    "Native Config::path and index/namespace/handle Views, complete canonical ancestor enumeration, create_dir_all behavior and the aggregate repair-to-durable-absence correspondence remain separate implementation obligations. The actual loop proof does not prove the enumerated paths are complete or that a syscall acts on their intended directory.",
    "ENV-DIRECTORY supplies individual barrier durability and stable accessible namespace identities. File-system internals, aliases/mount rebinding and arbitrary callback mutation are not verified.",
    "Existing gc_batch/gc_receipt/WAL proofs and same-client/reopen tests cover deletion/sync/receipt errors and retries under their declared contracts. Complete native catalog context, all application roots, distributed protocol composition, discovery/retry progress and crashed-writer fencing remain open.",
    "No straw implementation body was admitted or replaced with an assumed equivalent; actual dispatch bodies are shared between native Rust and Verus. Allocation, compiler and standard-library correctness retain their existing trusted boundaries."
  ],
